# Fixes a real bug in pestphp/pest-plugin-browser 4.3.1's
# Page::expectScreenshot(): once the strict, byte-exact
# expect($actual)->toMatchSnapshot() check fails (which routinely happens
# on ordinary render-timing/font-antialiasing jitter, even for a visually
# identical screenshot -- expected, and exactly why the tolerant fallback
# below exists), the fallback catch block has no success path at all.
#
# Confirmed directly from Playwright's own driver source
# (node_modules/playwright-core/lib/coreBundle.js, Page.expectScreenshot):
#   - On a genuine mismatch beyond threshold, the driver throws
#     server-side. Client::execute() (Client.php) already turns this into
#     an ExpectationFailedException with Playwright's own message before
#     Page.php's result-handling loop is ever reached.
#   - On a genuine pass within threshold, the driver returns `{}` -- no
#     `diff` key, ever.
#
# But Page::expectScreenshot()'s loop only handles "a message carried
# result.diff" (real mismatch). If the loop finishes without ever seeing a
# diff key -- exactly what happens on a genuine pass -- it fell through to
# an unconditional failure (a placeholder "missing image" diff view plus
# the same canned "Screenshot does not match the last one" message),
# regardless of what the tolerant comparison actually determined.
#
# Live proof (piwigo17-rewrite, 2026-07-17): a failing "search" VR test's
# embedded "actual" screenshot decoded to be MD5-identical to its baseline
# .snap file -- a confirmed pass, reported as a failure.
#
# This patch removes the unconditional fallback failure and lets the
# method fall through to its implicit `void` return once the loop
# completes without finding a diff, since that state is only reachable
# after Playwright's own driver already determined the screenshots match.
--- a/src/Playwright/Page.php	2026-04-08 18:04:12.000000000 -0300
+++ b/src/Playwright/Page.php	2026-07-17 23:15:09.068360086 -0300
@@ -550,19 +550,19 @@
                 }
             }
 
-            $this->createImageDiffView(
-                $snapshotName,
-                $expectedImageBlob,
-                $actualImageBlob,
-                ImageDiffView::missingImage(),
-                $openDiff,
-            );
-
-            throw new ExpectationFailedException(<<<'EOT'
-                Screenshot does not match the last one.
-                  - Expected? Update the snapshots with [--update-snapshots].
-                EOT,
-            );
+            // No message carried a `result.diff`. Playwright's own driver
+            // (playwright-core's Page.expectScreenshot handler) returns an
+            // empty result (`{}`) when the screenshot matches within the
+            // threshold/maxDiffPixels/maxDiffPixelRatio options passed
+            // above, and throws server-side on a genuine mismatch instead
+            // -- which Client::execute() already turns into an
+            // ExpectationFailedException before this loop is ever reached.
+            // Reaching this point therefore means the tolerant comparison
+            // passed: the strict, byte-exact toMatchSnapshot() above is
+            // far more sensitive than the comparator (any render-timing/
+            // anti-aliasing jitter fails it even when the image is
+            // visually identical). Falling through to a hardcoded failure
+            // here was reporting these passes as flaky test failures.
         }
     }
 
